          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مقهى (maqhā) is a place noun made from qahwa, \"coffee\". In Lane qahwa is an old word for wine, and he notes that coffee is now called by it; his lexicon has no article on q-h-w itself."
            }
          ]
